  "theorem": "For every primitive ordinal and every nine-tuple of natural-register values, relate the two source configurations by identical ordinal and register store. Equal operations and operands give equal guards, updates and halt decisions. The exhaustive equality of every guarded successor gives equal next ordinals. This is a strong step-for-step bisimulation, and therefore preserves halting from every corresponding source configuration, without a bound on register values or run length.",
